================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTIONS
================================================================================

The list below covers the complete runtime dependency closure of the `mycad`
distribution, as enumerated by:

    uv tree --package mycad --no-dev

Development-only tooling (ruff, basedpyright, pytest, pytest-cov, hatchling,
editables) is declared in a PEP 735 dependency group, is not part of the
runtime closure, and is therefore not listed here.

Each license identifier below was taken from the installed distribution's
own metadata (the `License` / `License-Expression` field, or the
`License :: ...` trove classifier). Where metadata was absent or
non-specific, the identifier was read from the distribution's bundled
license file; those cases are marked with the evidence path.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenCascade Technology (OCCT) — dual attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `cadquery-ocp-novtk` wheel contains two separately licensed bodies of work
and is therefore attributed on two lines:

  cadquery-ocp-novtk (OCP binding code)   Apache-2.0
      Source: distribution METADATA `License: Apache-2.0`.

  Open CASCADE Technology 7.9.3 (bundled)  LGPL-2.1 with the Open CASCADE
                                           exception
      The wheel ships 46 prebuilt OCCT shared libraries under
      `cadquery_ocp_novtk.libs/` (libTKernel, libTKFillet, libTKBRep, ...).
      These are separate native libraries loaded dynamically at runtime; they
      are NOT a derivative work of MyCAD source. Upstream OCCT is distributed
      under LGPL-2.1 together with the Open CASCADE exception.
      Evidence boundary: the wheel does not ship an OCCT license text, and its
      `dist-info/sboms/auditwheel.cdx.json` enumerates only the system
      libraries absorbed by auditwheel (libfreeimage, libtiff, libopenexr and
      similar), not OCCT itself. The identifier above therefore reflects the
      upstream OCCT project terms rather than a statement found inside the
      wheel. Anyone redistributing MyCAD together with this wheel should
      satisfy the LGPL obligations for those native libraries.

